From e0d31d17a4e9df1c6d77ba59e2517a6f61aa9901 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:42:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: pciehp: Quirk broken Command Completed support on NordAU
 (SA8797P)

  Both root ports (0000:00:00.0, 0001:00:00.0) log a hotplug command
  timeout at boot and on every suspend/resume (s2idle) cycle:

    pcieport 0000:00:00.0: pciehp: Timeout on hotplug command 0x13f8 (issued 57216 msec ago)
    pcieport 0001:00:00.0: pciehp: Timeout on hotplug command 0x13f8 (issued 57244 msec ago)
    pcieport 0000:00:00.0: pciehp: Timeout on hotplug command 0x03d8 (issued 2020 msec ago)
    pcieport 0001:00:00.0: pciehp: Timeout on hotplug command 0x03d8 (issued 2020 msec ago)

  0x13f8 has HPIE+CCIE set, so the first command waits on the interrupt
  path (wait_event_timeout). 0x03d8 has HPIE clear, so the next command
  falls back to directly polling PCI_EXP_SLTSTA for Command Completed
  (pcie_poll_cmd()) -- and still times out. Since even direct polling of
  the status register never observes the CC bit, the root port's own
  Slot Status truly never reports Command Completed; this isn't an
  interrupt-routing problem. Both ports hit it identically, consistent
  with a controller-wide (silicon) trait rather than a per-slot anomaly.
  On resume this erratum alone accounts for ~2.8s of the ~3.4s spent
  getting Endpoint back online.

  This is the same class of erratum quirk_cmd_compl() already exists to
  work around for other Qualcomm root ports (0x010e, 0x0110, 0x0400,
  0x0401): the port advertises SLTCAP.HPC=1 but doesn't actually honor
  Command Completed. NordAU's (SA8797P) root port Device ID (0x011f) was
  missing from that fixup list, so pdev->broken_cmd_compl was never set
  and pciehp assumed real CC support, blocking on every command.

  Adding the fixup entry alone is not sufficient. broken_cmd_compl is
  only consulted by the CC_ERRATUM_MASK fast path in
  pcie_do_write_cmd(), which skips the wait only for commands that leave
  the Control bits (PCC/PIC/AIC/EIC) unchanged -- i.e. only Enable-bit-
  only writes (0x13f8-style). The fast path that fully disables waiting
  (NO_CMD_CMPL(), via SLTCAP.NCCS) was gated solely on
  pdev->is_thunderbolt, so writes that do touch Control bits (0x03d8-
  style) still fell through to the full wait/timeout regardless of
  broken_cmd_compl.

  Force NCCS for broken_cmd_compl controllers too, so NO_CMD_CMPL()
  skips the wait for every command on these controllers, not just
  Enable-bit-only ones. Verified against boot-KPI logs: with both
  changes, pciehp timeouts drop from 2 chained events per port to zero,
  and wake-to-Endpoint-ready time on resume drops from 3.350s to 0.541s.

Change-Id: I43dfea7aefc4d3b8265bf1208c12c8d0592b9663
Signed-off-by: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/pci/hotplug/pciehp_hpc.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/hotplug/pciehp_hpc.c b/drivers/pci/hotplug/pciehp_hpc.c
index b0bccc4d0da2..34d2b9418f8b 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/hotplug/pciehp_hpc.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/hotplug/pciehp_hpc.c
@@ -1000,6 +1000,18 @@ struct controller *pcie_init(struct pcie_device *dev)
 	if (pdev->is_thunderbolt)
 		slot_cap |= PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_NCCS;
 
+	/*
+	 * quirk_cmd_compl() sets broken_cmd_compl for controllers that
+	 * claim Command Completed support but never actually raise it,
+	 * regardless of which Slot Control bits are written. The
+	 * CC_ERRATUM_MASK fast path in pcie_do_write_cmd() only covers
+	 * writes that leave the Control bits (PCC/PIC/AIC/EIC) unchanged;
+	 * force NCCS here too so NO_CMD_CMPL() skips the wait entirely for
+	 * every command on these controllers, not just Enable-bit-only ones.
+	 */
+	if (pdev->broken_cmd_compl)
+		slot_cap |= PCI_EXP_SLTCAP_NCCS;
+
 	ctrl->slot_cap = slot_cap;
 	mutex_init(&ctrl->ctrl_lock);
 	mutex_init(&ctrl->state_lock);
@@ -1088,3 +1100,6 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0401,
 			      PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI, 8, quirk_cmd_compl);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_HXT, 0x0401,
 			      PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI, 8, quirk_cmd_compl);
+/* QCOM NordAU (SA8797P) root port */
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x011f,
+			      PCI_CLASS_BRIDGE_PCI, 8, quirk_cmd_compl);
-- 

